  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>Two vertices of a triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, and its&nbsp;centroid be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, let the vertex &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&#39;&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and using centroid formula we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>So, the third vertex will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now finding image of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Now find the required answer we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>74</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
